---
args: { input: CaseInput }
returns: RunProposal
---
1. Bind `goal = await frameRequest(input)` from the request and `policy = await selectPolicy(input)` from supplied authority candidates. Preserve unresolved precedence instead of guessing which source governs.
2. Bind `work = await formTaskGraph(goal)` and `evidencePlan = await planEvidence(input, work)` so each operation has explicit prerequisites and a searched source universe.
3. Run the stages in their dependency order. The first stage receives only `input.domainRecords.firstStage`; every later stage receives the preceding function's actual accepted records. Bind each full result separately.
const collectSymptomsResult = await collectSymptoms(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan);
const formMechanismsResult = await formMechanisms(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, collectSymptomsResult.accepted);
const designWorkPackagesResult = await designWorkPackages(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, formMechanismsResult.accepted);
const sequenceCampaignResult = await sequenceCampaign(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, designWorkPackagesResult.accepted);
const verifyImprovementResult = await verifyImprovement(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, sequenceCampaignResult.accepted);
4. Bind `stageSet: CaseStageSet = { collectSymptoms: collectSymptomsResult, formMechanisms: formMechanismsResult, designWorkPackages: designWorkPackagesResult, sequenceCampaign: sequenceCampaignResult, verifyImprovement: verifyImprovementResult }` and `collection: CollectionFinding = await reconcileCollection(stageSet)`. Bind `allQuestions: string[] = [...collectSymptomsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...formMechanismsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...designWorkPackagesResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...sequenceCampaignResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...verifyImprovementResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...collection.coverageGaps]` and `questions: QuestionBatch = await resolveQuestions(allQuestions, input)`.
5. Bind `invalidation = await assessDelta(input)`, `review = await prepareReview(collection)`, and `view = await composeView(review, input)`; pass each child its actual declared inputs and retain the returned object.
6. Bind `allChecks: CheckResult[] = [...collectSymptomsResult.checks, ...formMechanismsResult.checks, ...designWorkPackagesResult.checks, ...sequenceCampaignResult.checks, ...verifyImprovementResult.checks]`. Bind `hasGateFailure = allChecks.some(check => check.verdict !== "pass")` and `hasBlocker = input.authorityStatus !== "authorized" || questions.questions.length > 0 || collection.coverageGaps.length > 0`. Bind `disposition: "proposed" | "blocked" | "needs-review" = hasBlocker ? "blocked" : hasGateFailure ? "needs-review" : "proposed"`. Bind `rationale: string[] = allChecks.map(check => `${check.check}: ${check.verdict}; evidence ${check.evidenceIds.join(",")}`)`.
7. Operational detail 1 — A cleanup removes an undocumented integration: require consumer discovery before deletion. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (require consumer discovery before deletion.) through the existing stage result for DebtSymptom; preserve exact source/version and the prior DebtSymptom, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
8. Operational detail 2 — A campaign spans teams: assign interface ownership and acceptance explicitly. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (assign interface ownership and acceptance explicitly.) through the existing stage result for DebtSymptom; preserve exact source/version and the prior DebtSymptom, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
9. Operational detail 3 — A metric improves because usage fell: preserve exposure and workload denominators. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (preserve exposure and workload denominators.) through the existing stage result for DebtSymptom; preserve exact source/version and the prior DebtSymptom, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
10. Operational detail 4 — A package grows during discovery: rebaseline scope rather than hiding an expanding rewrite. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (rebaseline scope rather than hiding an expanding rewrite.) through the existing stage result for DebtSymptom; preserve exact source/version and the prior DebtSymptom, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
11. Operational detail 5 — A workaround is retired: verify all dependent runbooks and alerts are updated. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (verify all dependent runbooks and alerts are updated.) through the existing stage result for DebtSymptom; preserve exact source/version and the prior DebtSymptom, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
12. Initialize `revisions: RevisionProposal[] = []`. If any gate is not pass, bind `revision = await proposeRevision(the failed check names, the smallest affected stage name)` and add that returned proposal to revisions. Bind and return `result: RunProposal = { caseId: input.caseId, goal, policy, work, evidencePlan, collectSymptoms: collectSymptomsResult, formMechanisms: formMechanismsResult, designWorkPackages: designWorkPackagesResult, sequenceCampaign: sequenceCampaignResult, verifyImprovement: verifyImprovementResult, collection, questions, invalidation, review, view, revisions, disposition, rationale }`. Proposed actions remain proposals. The host owns authorization, persistence, effect dispatch and verification.
